module gunbc.factory_attempt_execution_on_fabric_audit

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, Bool, Int, List }

data factory_attempt_execution_on_fabric_audit_note: String = "FIRST-SLICE AUDIT of the roadmap node factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority, the row whose id is factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease; extraction 3943 bytes, sha256 4a0fd2bbf0b1da5a30eeec160ab2d5ab49478cae26d5e75d6cb104b121bd6802 at origin/main 65230868362de3efc0ddfeeaeef5d83eeb2fa385, byte-identical to 8b434ce74d6c). The row's first_slice: enumerate every state the belt holds that execution reads at start, and map each to the fabric record that already carries it or name it as needing one — that mapping is factory_attempt_state_mappings below; its disposition column carries a per-row RECOMMENDATION beside the evidence, while the decision itself lives in the operator's realization-home ruling (THE HOME OF THE DECISION, below — this module decides nothing).

This is NOT the node's closing contract and is NOT bound to the node's acceptance — the same distinction the operator's 2026-08-02 ruling forced on gunbc.materialization_kernel_closing_frontier_audit (renamed off '...closing_contract' for exactly this reason). A Delivered verdict is a CLAIM ABOUT A WITNESS THAT WAS RUN; authored verdicts cannot lift a rung (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder rung honesty, gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed). Every verdict below was authored by the audit slice (session fierce-wren-253) from a source read at 65230868362d under the G0 contained-development-execution gate: NO witness was executed in this slice, so no clause reads Delivered here, and factory_attempt_all_clauses_delivered evaluates false by construction rather than vacuously passing.

Citation discipline (DESIGN.md reading rules): the symbol is load-bearing, the line number is convenience. Every line number was read at 65230868362d; after a rebase the symbol still names the fact."

type FactoryAuditVerdict
  = NotDelivered { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | PartiallyDelivered { reason: NonEmptyStr, evidence: NonEmptyStr }
  | Delivered { witness_module: NonEmptyStr, witness_fn: NonEmptyStr, evidence: NonEmptyStr }

type FactoryAuditClause {
  id: NonEmptyStr
  statement: NonEmptyStr
  verdict: FactoryAuditVerdict
}

// THE CONSUMER, named (gunbc.design_argument::consumption — a declaration nothing consumes is dangling,
// however well modeled): the paired witness dag/test/claim/factory_attempt_execution_on_fabric_audit_witness.dag
// (module test.claim.factory_attempt_execution_on_fabric_audit_witness) exercises every projection below —
// the rung match, the clause fold, the per-id rung lookups, the mapping invariants and the per-row
// recommendation rung — and its test fns are the executing route (the CI witness floor). This is the same
// wiring the two repo audits have: gunbc.materialization_kernel_closing_frontier_audit is consumed only by
// test.claim.materialization_kernel_closing_frontier_audit_witness, and gunbc.expected_value_authority_audit
// only by test.claim.self_host_expected_value_authority_audit_witness.

data factory_attempt_consumer: String =
  "test.claim.factory_attempt_execution_on_fabric_audit_witness — its test fns read the clause fold, the " +
  "rung projections and the mapping invariants; executed by the CI witness floor."

// THE HOME OF THE DECISION (gunbc.design_argument::planning_has_one_home — a plan's authority is its .dag
// carrier under gunbc.plans, the work that realizes it lives under gunbc.roadmap; a second place that
// decides what is planned is a fork): this module carries AUDIT FINDINGS only. The realization-home
// decision the disposition column recommends toward is the operator's ruling, recorded in
// gunbc.design_ruling; the red controls and their staffing (witness module + fn, red_at / green_at) are
// work-item facts on node://adhoc-de172383-0e3 and its edges in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority. Nothing
// below decides, schedules or staffs anything; the disposition arms are per-row recommendations beside
// their evidence, and this module deliberately cites the row's red_control only by NUMBER (red control (1)
// / (2) / (3), defined in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority), never restating its text as its own planning
// fact (DESIGN.md 'Planning has one home': a planning fact the model already carries is not restated as a
// field beside it).

data factory_attempt_decision_home: String = "decision: the operator's realization-home ruling (gunbc.design_ruling; Hold is the default). staffing: work item node://adhoc-de172383-0e3 and the roadmap row's own red_control in gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority. This module holds neither."

// The ONE exhaustive match on FactoryAuditVerdict in this module (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority —
// an undeclared sum re-matched by a family of free predicates duplicates the same exhaustiveness fact at
// each call site). Rungs: 0 NotDelivered, 1 PartiallyDelivered, 2 Delivered. Every rung question —
// delivered, partially delivered, not delivered — derives from this one match.

fn factory_attempt_verdict_rung(v: FactoryAuditVerdict) -> Int {
  match v {
    NotDelivered { reason: _ } => 0
    PartiallyDelivered { reason: _, evidence: _ } => 1
    Delivered { witness_module: _, witness_fn: _, evidence: _ } => 2
  }
}

fn factory_attempt_clause_rung(c: FactoryAuditClause) -> Int {
  factory_attempt_verdict_rung(v: c.verdict)
}

fn factory_attempt_clause_delivered(c: FactoryAuditClause) -> Bool {
  factory_attempt_clause_rung(c: c) == 2
}

fn factory_attempt_clause_count(clauses: List<FactoryAuditClause>) -> Int {
  count(clauses)
}

fn factory_attempt_progress_count(clauses: List<FactoryAuditClause>) -> Int {
  clauses |> filter(c => factory_attempt_clause_delivered(c: c)) |> count()
}

// The derived AUDIT SUMMARY: true only if every audited clause independently reached Delivered.
// Not a roadmap execution contract; see the note above.

fn factory_attempt_all_clauses_delivered(clauses: List<FactoryAuditClause>) -> Bool {
  clauses |> fold(init: true, f: (acc, c) => acc && factory_attempt_clause_delivered(c: c))
}

fn factory_attempt_clauses() -> List<FactoryAuditClause> {
  [
    FactoryAuditClause {
      id: "gap-is-real",
      statement: "The belt still owns attempt state on main: no commit since 2026-11-19 lands the node, and the belt-local slot store and the capture-owed refusal still read.",
      verdict: PartiallyDelivered {
        reason: "Source read at 65230868362d only; no witness executed under the G0 gate." as NonEmptyStr,
        evidence: "git log --since=2026-11-19 naming the node returned nothing (rc=0, empty output). belt_attempt_slots: 7 hits in dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_belt_actuate.dag (belt_attempt_slots_census :1616, census-with-carry-over :1663-:1669, belt_attempt_slots_cutover_pass :1671, sole caller :4792, tick pass fields :5198/:5217/:5235). CaptureOwed still minted at dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_attempt_continuation.dag:272 and consumed at :422." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FactoryAuditClause {
      id: "bug-10-nonce-is-not-a-generation-check",
      statement: "The drain starts an enqueued request without checking the placement lease's slot generation: the nonce the belt mints FROM the generation is opaque to the launch authority, so a lease released — or re-admitted at a newer generation — between enqueue and start still starts (srv1 lab defect 10).",
      verdict: PartiallyDelivered {
        reason: "Confirmed in source at 65230868362d; no witness exists that refuses on the generation, so nothing executed proves the refusal." as NonEmptyStr,
        evidence: "Mint: roadmap_belt_actuate.dag:1559 (nonce: to_string(value: cas_generation_count(g: launched.slot_generation))). Opaque use: dag/gunbc/roadmap/attempt_system_unit_launch.dag:226 comment, :233 field; consumers are ONLY path-segment safety at :560, echo at :574, non-empty at :632-633. A grep of that whole module for slot_generation, ExpectSlotGeneration and begin_launch returned rc=1 (zero hits). The drain path checks nothing about the lease: attempt_system_unit_process_claimed :1148 calls attempt_system_unit_cli_start :1055 calls attempt_system_unit_start_admitted :325, which checks user, argv program and byte bound only. The authority that already answers it: dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_session_placement.dag:541 session_placement_begin_launch carrying expected: grant.slot_generation at :542, consumed as ExpectSlotGeneration in dag/gunbc/compute/attempt_lifecycle.dag at :581, :710, :1144 (attempt_begin_launch :745, attempt_fenced_commit :1142)." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FactoryAuditClause {
      id: "bug-4-capture-owed-waits-forever",
      statement: "An attempt that ended with capture owed and has no commit-step record for its head is refused forever: CaptureNotAttempted maps to Refuse with cause CaptureOwed, and the only thing that ever bounded the wait is a belt-side commit record that may never exist (srv1 lab defect 4).",
      verdict: PartiallyDelivered {
        reason: "Confirmed in source at 65230868362d; the existing witness LOCKS the wait-forever behaviour, so it is evidence for the defect, not for the cut." as NonEmptyStr,
        evidence: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_attempt_continuation.dag:272 declares the RefuseCause variant CaptureOwed { reason: String }; :422 maps CaptureNotAttempted to Refuse whose text says CONTINUE waits for that capture. The bound is belt_capture_absence_for_attempt (roadmap_belt_actuate.dag:8614), which reads AttemptCommitOutcomeLast and maps an absent file to CaptureNotAttempted (:8616) or owed to CaptureNotAttempted (:8619); belt_claim_capture_of :1823 turns that into ClaimCaptureOwed at :1830. dag/test/claim/roadmap/roadmap_attempt_continuation_witness.dag:282 owed_capture_refuses_and_never_spawns_from_branch_head pins the refusal, and its comment at :274-:279 states boundedness rests ONLY on the commit lane reading the commit record." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FactoryAuditClause {
      id: "cutover-pass-is-ungated",
      statement: "belt_attempt_slots_cutover_pass runs on every belt tick with no gate: it is bound before the wholesale-withholding match and carried in BOTH returned arms, so a withheld tick still executes the roadmap-local migration write.",
      verdict: PartiallyDelivered {
        reason: "Confirmed in source at 65230868362d; the witnesses near the pass observe it, none gate it." as NonEmptyStr,
        evidence: "roadmap_belt_actuate.dag:1671 belt_attempt_slots_cutover_pass (record_write at :1686; outcomes AttemptSlotsCutoverCarried :1700 and AttemptSlotsCutoverAlreadyCarried :1704); sole caller :4792 inside belt_tick_for_instance, bound BEFORE the match on belt_tick_wholesale_of and returned in both arms — TickPassesWithheld at :4801 carries slots_cutover: slots_cutover at :4810, the full TickPasses at :4821. The witnesses in dag/test/claim/roadmap/roadmap_belt_actuate_witness.dag at :3395 and :3416 decode cutover receipts; neither gates the pass." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FactoryAuditClause {
      id: "metering-has-no-fabric-or-compute-authority",
      statement: "Usage metering has no fabric or compute counterpart, so the cut has no record to migrate it onto: metering is the clearest RE-HOME and the ruling this audit feeds must name its home.",
      verdict: PartiallyDelivered {
        reason: "Absence confirmed by grep at 65230868362d only; where the home should be is the operator's realization-home ruling, not this audit's call." as NonEmptyStr,
        evidence: "grep of 'etering' across dag/product, src/v2/product/fabric, src/v2/product/capacity, dag/gunbc/fabric and dag/gunbc/compute returned only dag/product/data_class.dag:27 and dag/product/data_category.dag:69, :266, :387 (rc=0) — prose mentions, no metering record; the searches for a metering type under those authorities found nothing else. The whole surface lives in dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_attempt_metering.dag (module gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_metering; MeteredRole :70, AttemptMeteringRecord :103, metering_standing_of :425, attempt_metering_decode :860), consumed by roadmap_belt_actuate.dag:23, roadmap_service_evidence.dag:9 and roadmap_dogfood_route.dag:17." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FactoryAuditClause {
      id: "consistent-with-the-two-parent-rows",
      statement: "The mapping is consistent with the node's two parents at main: execution-attempt-one-record (product.fabric.execution Attempt and ExecutionAttemptLineage canonical; the belt's attempt state migrates THROUGH this node) and venue-contract (every executor on one accept-report-consume contract over product.fabric.execution).",
      verdict: PartiallyDelivered {
        reason: "Consistency argued from the rows and the records at 65230868362d. The one place it CANNOT be consistent is metering: neither parent row declares a usage record, so that clause says so plainly rather than claiming a home." as NonEmptyStr,
        evidence: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_authority.dag:912 execution-attempt-one-record states 'The belt's own attempt state is migrated by factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease, which consumes this record'; :976 venue-contract requires accepting a committed fill and refusing a stale or foreign one; the edges exist at :8100-:8101. The records are there to be migrated onto: dag/product/fabric/execution.dag ExecutionAttemptLineage :39, Attempt<P> :51 carrying lineage at :54, LeaseIdentity :66, Receipt<P> :172, grant_lease_generation :194, ReceiptAdmission :226, admit_receipt_for_grant :233. venue-contract's own red control — a fill for a superseded generation is refused — is exactly the check that routes bug 10 through the ExpectSlotGeneration CAS cited above." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FactoryAuditClause {
      id: "audit-can-fail",
      statement: "This audit can read false: factory_attempt_all_clauses_delivered over factory_attempt_clauses() evaluates false on the rows above, so the summary is not a vacuously green AND over authored data.",
      verdict: PartiallyDelivered {
        reason: "The paired witness exists in this change and the CI witness floor executes it, which is what proves the fold reads false rather than being an always-true wrapper; the rung climbs to Delivered once that execution is cited here as the observation. Until the CI run for this head is recorded beside the clause, the rung stays at PartiallyDelivered — fail-closed on an unexecuted claim (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed)." as NonEmptyStr,
        evidence: "dag/test/claim/factory_attempt_execution_on_fabric_audit_witness.dag::factory_attempt_audit_fold_reads_false_proves_can_fail asserts the fold over these exact rows == false; test.claim.factory_attempt_execution_on_fabric_audit_witness is the executing route." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
  ]
}

// THE MAPPING — the first_slice itself. One row per piece of belt-, attempt-, dispatch- or session-
// module state that execution reads at start: (a) what execution needs from it, (b) which fabric or
// compute authority already answers it (module and symbol, with the line read at 65230868362d), and
// (c) the disposition when the cut lands. Delete = a fabric/compute authority answers it and the
// roadmap copy goes. ReHome = no authority answers it; a record must be NAMED, and that column is the
// decision the realization-home ruling carries. Keep = host transport, not lease state.

type FactoryStateDisposition
  = Delete { because: NonEmptyStr }
  | ReHome { needs: NonEmptyStr }
  | Keep { why: NonEmptyStr }

type FactoryStateMapping {
  belt_module: NonEmptyStr
  state: NonEmptyStr
  read_at_start: NonEmptyStr
  fabric_authority: NonEmptyStr
  disposition: FactoryStateDisposition
}

// The ONE exhaustive match on FactoryStateDisposition (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority): 0 Delete,
// 1 ReHome, 2 Keep. Rung questions about a recommendation derive from this match alone.

fn factory_attempt_disposition_rung(d: FactoryStateDisposition) -> Int {
  match d {
    Delete { because: _ } => 0
    ReHome { needs: _ } => 1
    Keep { why: _ } => 2
  }
}

fn factory_attempt_mapping_disposition_rung(m: FactoryStateMapping) -> Int {
  factory_attempt_disposition_rung(d: m.disposition)
}

fn factory_attempt_state_mappings() -> List<FactoryStateMapping> {
  [
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_state_store" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "AttemptStateMember (roadmap_attempt_state_store.dag:61, 25 file members) read and written per attempt through attempt_state_observe_at :301, attempt_state_read_at :323, attempt_state_write_at :354, under the belt-attempt root" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "the launch decision reads key, fingerprint, launch identity, spawn origin, environment admission and publication receipt before it starts anything (roadmap_belt_actuate.dag:3598, :5351 and :5356, :5632 and :5638, :5912 and :5926; write :5955)" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle carries the IDENTITY half: AttemptState :127 and AttemptRecord :203 (identity, reference, unit, granted, opened_at, launch_deadline, state, owner) behind AttemptPayloadCodec :444" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: ReHome {
        needs: "Split: the identity/spawn members (AttemptKeyRecord, AttemptProcessFingerprint, AttemptLaunchIdentity, AttemptSpawnOrigin, AttemptEnvironmentAdmission, AttemptSpawnFailure) answer attempt_lifecycle questions and DELETE with the slot record; the work-product members (verification, review, oracle, publication, diff, validation — the majority of the 25) answer NO attempt-lifecycle question and have no fabric record at all. They need a named record, or a ruling that they are worker output living outside the attempt record." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_state_store" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "AttemptLogMember (roadmap_attempt_state_store.dag:107, 6 append lanes: worker events, verification retry entries, oracle revisions, spawn failures)" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "the continuation reads the prior worker's event log before planning (PriorExecutionObservation feeding continuation_plan :334)" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log is the typed append authority: event_log_append_with :192, event_log_read_partition :178" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: ReHome { needs: "the six lanes onto fabric event-log partitions; the file-directory log lanes DELETE after the migration — two histories for one attempt violates single authority (DESIGN.md, 'Single authority', :210-:225)" as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the belt's attempt slot census and carry-over: belt_attempt_slots_census :1616, belt_attempt_slots_census_with_carry_over :1669, and the record written by belt_attempt_slots_cutover_pass :1671 (record_write :1686)" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "belt_tick_for_instance :4792 binds the pass before any gate; the withheld tick still carries it (:4810, :4821)" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "the slot store is ALREADY the shared layer: gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle attempt_slot_keys :401, read_attempt_slot :406, write_attempt_slot :414 over gunbc.compute.compute_attempt_slots_root (slot_root_path :46), with ExpectSlotGeneration consumed at :581, :710, :1144" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: Delete { because: "red control (3): no module may run belt_attempt_slots_cutover_pass or keep a roadmap-local slot store; the census reads the shared root instead" as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the start sequence belt_session_container_create :1511-:1590: placement record write :1548, session_placement_begin_launch CAS :1552, start-request nonce mint :1559, queue enqueue :1563, drain read via harness_start_from_observation :1576" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "this IS the start path, and the nonce at :1559 is the only generation-bound value that reaches the host — where nothing reads it as a generation (bug 10)" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "roadmap_session_placement.dag:481 session_placement_acquire and :541 session_placement_begin_launch (expected: grant.slot_generation at :542) over product.capacity.lease LeaseGrant (imported at :7) and attempt_lifecycle attempt_begin_launch :745" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: Delete { because: "the nonce mint at :1559 and the belt's extra placement copy go once the drain admits through ExpectSlotGeneration — the bug-10 fix; begin_launch already delegates to the shared CAS" as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.attempt_system_unit_launch" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the host start queue: attempt_system_unit_request_path :261 and entries carrying node, attempt key, grant, argv, ordinal and the opaque nonce :233, claimed by the systemd drain" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "the drain's claim IS the start: attempt_system_unit_process_claimed :1148 to attempt_system_unit_cli_start :1055 to attempt_system_unit_start_admitted :325 checks user, argv program and byte bound, and nothing about the lease" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "the accept-side authority exists but is unused here: product.capacity.lease LeaseFence :27, fence_verdict :42, lease_grant_expired_at :81, and the ExpectSlotGeneration CAS in gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle :581, :710, :1144" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: Keep { why: "the queue is host transport, not lease state. The cut ADDS the generation check at claim, through the shared CAS — it does not delete the queue. venue-contract's refuse-a-stale-fill control is where that check belongs." as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_continuation" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the capture-owed standing: RefuseCause CaptureOwed :272, produced by continuation_plan :334 at :422 whenever capture is CaptureNotAttempted" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "the belt will not start a new attempt for a node while a prior attempt's capture is owed — forever when no commit-step record exists (bug 4)" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "a terminal Receipt is the record that already answers how an attempt ended: product.fabric.execution Receipt<P> :172, the claim receipt_terminal_binds_lease :219, admit_receipt_for_grant :233" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: Delete { because: "red control (2): capture re-run on any attempt, including one predating commit-step records, must reach the SAME terminal outcome and never rest owed. The refusal arm goes with the belt-local commit record, replaced by receipt admission; the witness at roadmap_attempt_continuation_witness.dag:282 that pins the wait-forever must be recut in the same PR." as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the commit step's outcome record: AttemptCommitOutcomeLast observed by belt_capture_absence_for_attempt :8614 and persisted by belt_commit_outcome_persist :8629 (write :8638), with the capture disposition at :8508 and :8602" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "it is the ONLY thing bounding CaptureOwed — an attempt whose record is absent is refused forever" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "product.fabric.execution Receipt<P> :172 admitted by admit_receipt_for_grant :233 — the terminal record is receipt admission, not a belt file" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: Delete { because: "the Receipt takes over the question; belt_capture_absence_for_attempt and belt_claim_capture_of :1823 (ClaimCaptureOwed :1830) go with the file" as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the worktree claim: attempt_worktree_claim_new :133, its codec :160, open/close returning AttemptTransition :194, keyed on AttemptKeyRecord :23 and :78" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "the launch admits the claim before spawn so two attempts never share a worktree" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "ALREADY on the shared layer: gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle AttemptPayloadCodec :444 with the fenced transitions attempt_fenced_prepare :1130 and attempt_fenced_commit :1142" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: Delete { because: "only the roadmap-local store ROOT is roadmap-local (worktree_claim_store root_of :191, store :210); the claim itself needs no migration — the cheapest line of the cut" as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_metering" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the per-attempt metering record: MeteredRole :70, AttemptMeteringRecord :103, metering_standing_of :425, sealed-roster decode :849, attempt_metering_decode :860" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "the belt reads standing before admitting work (import at roadmap_belt_actuate.dag:23, per-attempt record at :8670); roadmap_service_evidence.dag:9 and roadmap_dogfood_route.dag:17 consume the same record" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "NONE — grep of 'etering' across dag/product, src/v2/product/fabric, src/v2/product/capacity, dag/gunbc/fabric and dag/gunbc/compute returns only prose in data_class.dag:27 and data_category.dag:69/:266/:387 (rc=0)" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: ReHome {
        needs: "THE decision this audit feeds. Neither parent row declares a usage record — execution-attempt-one-record canonicalizes identity, venue-contract covers accept/report — so the cut cannot land metering on any existing authority. The realization-home ruling must either name a usage record on product.fabric.execution or rule metering provider-side and re-home it under gunbc.compute beside the seat authority (fabric_seat_acquire :403, fabric_seat_release :654)." as NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_exit_spool" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the per-attempt exit spool: attempt_exit_spool_path :115, clear_attempt_exit_spool_dir :281, consumed by the belt via the import at roadmap_belt_actuate.dag:366 (clear path :3960)" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "the drain clears the spool around start so a reaped attempt's ending is not read as the new attempt's" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "NONE for the spooled bytes; fabric authority covers the RELEASE: fabric_seat_release :654 in gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log and compute_seat_discharge :393 in gunbc.compute.compute_seat_ensure" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: ReHome { needs: "the spool is drain-side host plumbing carrying terminal evidence; venue-contract asks for termination evidence on cancel. The ruling must say whether it rides onto the Receipt payload or stays a compute-side host effect beside the drain." as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_attempt_store_root" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the belt-attempt file root: belt_attempt_root_reading :105 with entry kinds including submission capture :192 and capture intent :209 and :226" as NonEmptyStr,
      read_at_start: "the capture and intent files under this root decide what the belt believes is captured before it starts the next attempt" as NonEmptyStr,
      fabric_authority: "product.fabric.execution Receipt<P> :172 (a capture IS a receipt) and the shared slot root gunbc.compute.compute_attempt_slots_root :46" as NonEmptyStr,
      disposition: Delete { because: "the root goes once receipts carry capture and slots live in the shared root; red control (3) forbids keeping the roadmap-local store" as NonEmptyStr }
    },
    FactoryStateMapping {
      belt_module: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_identity_store_root" as NonEmptyStr,
      state: "the attempt-identity store root: belt_attempt_identity_store_root :11 (root_of :48, store :64)" as NonEmptyStr,
